  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Near Place du Pin, between Place Garibaldi and the harbour, Babbo Mio is an Italian trattoria (spaghetti, seared tuna, pizzas, pasta, meats). The official website announces around sixty covers indoors and almost as many on a large terrace on the square; the tourist office counts 110 on the terrace. There is no takeaway (a doggy bag is offered if the plate is not finished) and no reservations, except for groups of more than 10 people: in the evening and at weekends, the restaurant advises coming early.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Two official sources contradict each other. The frequently asked questions of the restaurant's website (babbomio.com) say: "Yes, we welcome dogs, we simply ask that you keep them on a leash!" The Nice Côte d'Azur tourist office listing (French and English versions) states on the contrary that pets are not accepted. Neither specifies whether the rule applies to the dining room or the terrace.</p>
      <p><strong>Check before you go:</strong> call the restaurant on 04 93 14 90 73 to confirm whether your dog is accepted, and on the terrace or in the dining room, before going.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: if you come with your dog, arrive early (no reservations) and ask on arrival whether it can sit on the terrace, on a leash.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Place Garibaldi and the harbour of Nice are close by, according to the restaurant's website.</p>
    </div>

